Code derived from DOLFIN
========================

DOLFIN 2019.2 (https://bitbucket.org/fenics-project/dolfin), Copyright (C) 2008-2015
Anders Logg, Ola Skavhaug, Garth N. Wells and others, is LGPL-3.0-or-later:

- feluga/cpp/dof_reorder_star.cpp: `DofMapBuilder::compute_node_reordering`, copied and
  keeping its header, with the reordering graph a star a cell instead of a clique; moved
  from stokes-beadpack.
- feluga/plaza_periodic.py: `PlazaRefinementND`'s `face_long_edge`, `enforce_rules` and
  `do_refine`, reproduced in its C++ source with the periodic identification added to
  `enforce_rules`, ties of the longest edge broken by position, and frozen edges; moved
  from stokes-beadpack.

Code derived from fenicstools
=============================

The following files come from fenicstools (https://github.com/mikaem/fenicstools),
Copyright (C) 2011-2013 Mikael Mortensen <mikaem@math.uio.no>; each carries a copyright
line and `SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-or-later`:

- feluga/probes.py and feluga/cpp/Probe.{h,cpp}, Probes.{h,cpp}, GradProbe.{h,cpp},
  GradProbes.{h,cpp}, ProbeCollection.h, probe11.cpp: moved from addictif
  (addictif/common/fenicstools), whose copy is a modified fork of fenicstools' Probes.
  Relative to upstream it adds GradProbe and GradProbes and constructors that reuse
  already-located probes, and drops StatisticsProbe(s). feluga changes: the
  collection code Probes and GradProbes share is in ProbeCollection.h; cppimport builds
  cpp/probe11.cpp from the file's own path at the first use of Probe(s) or
  GradProbe(s); a dump's files are listed (filename.probes) and read back by read_dump.
- feluga/gradient.py and feluga/cpp/gradient_weight.cpp: from upstream fenicstools
  commit 03657ff (fenicstools/WeightedGradient.py and fenicstools/fem/gradient_weight.cpp).
  feluga changes: the module is compiled from the file's own path, on rank 0 of the
  caller's communicator; `compute_weighted_gradient_matrix` and
  `compute_DG0_to_CG_weight_matrix` are exposed at module level;
  `weighted_gradient_matrix` takes a direction or a tuple of them, building the
  averaging matrix once; the cell weights are summed on owned cells only, a ghost cell
  being its owner's, and exchanged between the ranks by all-to-all where upstream looked
  each dof's owner up.

Upstream's licence statements differ. The file headers say
`__license__ = "GNU Lesser GPL version 3 or any later version"` (Probe.py,
WeightedGradient.py), and setup.py has the classifier
`License :: OSI Approved :: GNU Library or Lesser General Public License (LGPL)`;
README.md, section "Licence", says "fenicstools is licensed under the GNU GPL,
version 3 or (at your option) any later version." feluga follows the file headers:
LGPL-3.0-or-later.
